WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.667 --> 00:00:04.033
-The committee investigating
the coup attempt on January 6th

00:00:04.033 --> 00:00:06.133
held what could
well be its final

00:00:06.133 --> 00:00:07.434
investigative hearing today

00:00:07.434 --> 00:00:08.968
in which they took
the dramatic step

00:00:08.968 --> 00:00:11.033
of voting to subpoena
Donald Trump.

00:00:11.033 --> 00:00:13.901
They also hinted at possible
criminal referrals

00:00:13.901 --> 00:00:15.501
for key figures
involved in the coup

00:00:15.501 --> 00:00:17.567
and revealed damning new
evidence from the Secret Service

00:00:17.567 --> 00:00:20.367
corroborating key details
about the insurrection.

00:00:20.367 --> 00:00:22.267
For more on this,
it's time for a closer look.

00:00:22.267 --> 00:00:24.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:26.501 --> 00:00:29.801
Just minutes before we came
out here to tape the show,

00:00:29.801 --> 00:00:31.300
the committee
concluded its hearing

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:33.234
with one of its most
stunning developments yet.

00:00:33.234 --> 00:00:36.367
They voted to subpoena
Donald Trump himself.

00:00:36.367 --> 00:00:38.667
-That concludes what may be
the committee's final

00:00:38.667 --> 00:00:40.934
public hearing
or meeting at least

00:00:40.934 --> 00:00:42.934
before the midterm elections.

00:00:42.934 --> 00:00:44.534
Their closing argument,
if you will,

00:00:44.534 --> 00:00:46.067
and it ended in dramatic fashion

00:00:46.067 --> 00:00:47.868
with the committee voting,
as you just heard,

00:00:47.868 --> 00:00:50.167
to subpoena
former President Trump

00:00:50.167 --> 00:00:52.334
to come testify before them.

00:00:52.334 --> 00:00:56.501
-On this vote, there are
nine ayes and zero nos.

00:00:56.501 --> 00:00:58.667
-The resolution is agreed to.

00:00:58.667 --> 00:01:00.567
-Now, they subpoenaed him,

00:01:00.567 --> 00:01:03.934
but can you imagine Donald Trump
complying with a subpoena

00:01:03.934 --> 00:01:05.467
from the January 6th committee?

00:01:05.467 --> 00:01:07.734
Watching him testify
before Congress would be insane.

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:10.334
He'd go on all sorts of
insane rants and attack people.

00:01:10.334 --> 00:01:12.634
It would be like
casting an actual lion

00:01:12.634 --> 00:01:14.033
in "The Lion King."

00:01:14.033 --> 00:01:15.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:16.634
Yeah, it was cool for a second,

00:01:16.634 --> 00:01:18.767
but then he clogged
Rudy Giuliani's face off.

00:01:18.767 --> 00:01:20.100
[ As Giuliani ]
It's okay, boss.

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:21.400
I don't need a face anyway.

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:22.868
I'll just draw on a new one.

00:01:22.868 --> 00:01:24.334
So...

00:01:24.334 --> 00:01:27.067
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.067 --> 00:01:28.934
Again, this news
broke late, guys.

00:01:28.934 --> 00:01:31.267
Our our graphics team --

00:01:32.267 --> 00:01:33.901
So it'll be fascinating
to see what happens

00:01:33.901 --> 00:01:34.901
with the Trump subpoena.

00:01:34.901 --> 00:01:36.734
But it was definitely necessary

00:01:36.734 --> 00:01:38.634
because as we've said
many times before,

00:01:38.634 --> 00:01:39.801
the reason why it's so important

00:01:39.801 --> 00:01:41.300
to investigate
the last coup attempt,

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:42.801
because the next one
is already underway.

00:01:42.801 --> 00:01:44.601
In fact, Trump still
reminisces publicly

00:01:44.601 --> 00:01:46.567
about January 6th
as if it was a good thing.

00:01:46.567 --> 00:01:48.801
Over the weekend,
he campaigned in Nevada

00:01:48.801 --> 00:01:50.467
alongside the
GOP candidates for Senate

00:01:50.467 --> 00:01:52.400
and the governor there,
who, it should be noted,

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:54.601
both eagerly accepted
his endorsement

00:01:54.601 --> 00:01:56.567
and who are actively touting
their support for Trump.

00:01:56.567 --> 00:01:57.901
And during that rally,

00:01:57.901 --> 00:02:01.100
Trump compared the size
of the crowd of the event

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:03.501
to the one that stormed
the Capitol on January 6th.

00:02:03.501 --> 00:02:05.634
-Nobody ever had crowds
like we've had.

00:02:05.634 --> 00:02:10.400
In the history of our country,
nobody's ever had crowds --

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:12.133
You know, the biggest crowd
I've ever seen?

00:02:12.133 --> 00:02:13.434
-Texas!

00:02:13.434 --> 00:02:17.100
-January 6th.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:19.067
-And you never hear that.

00:02:19.067 --> 00:02:20.067
It was the biggest.

00:02:20.067 --> 00:02:21.200
And they were there --

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:23.367
They were there largely
to protest

00:02:23.367 --> 00:02:26.734
a corrupt and rigged
and stolen election.

00:02:26.734 --> 00:02:29.000
It's the biggest crowd,
and you never hear that.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:31.567
And you see very few pictures
of it, but they're there.

00:02:31.567 --> 00:02:35.133
That was the biggest crowd
I believe I've ever spoken to.

00:02:35.133 --> 00:02:37.133
-There's never been better proof

00:02:37.133 --> 00:02:40.467
that Trump isn't watching
the January 6th hearings

00:02:40.467 --> 00:02:44.234
than him saying,
you see very few pictures of it.

00:02:44.234 --> 00:02:48.234
Dude, they're showing
pictures of it all the time.

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:49.767
Also, I know I'm just
the talk show host,

00:02:49.767 --> 00:02:51.634
but can I enter that
last video clip of Trump

00:02:51.634 --> 00:02:52.901
as a piece of evidence?

00:02:52.901 --> 00:02:54.501
Because I'm pretty sure
what we just saw there,

00:02:54.501 --> 00:02:55.701
that's a confession.

00:02:55.701 --> 00:02:57.100
And sure, I could just
point this out

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:58.534
to someone who's
actually a lawyer,

00:02:58.534 --> 00:03:01.901
but I would love to be the one
to enter the evidence myself

00:03:01.901 --> 00:03:04.234
in an actual courtroom,
because then I could do my

00:03:04.234 --> 00:03:06.067
Southern lawyer character
I've been working on.

00:03:06.067 --> 00:03:08.133
I'd wear a white suit
and I'd say something like,

00:03:08.133 --> 00:03:10.200
[ Southern drawl ] "Apologies,
Congresswoman Cheney,

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:13.734
but I do declare
this man is guilty

00:03:13.734 --> 00:03:16.968
and I have the smoking gun
to prove it.

00:03:16.968 --> 00:03:20.734
I have in my position
a video tape, and I --"

00:03:20.734 --> 00:03:23.067
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.067 --> 00:03:28.567
At this point I will pause
for scattered gasps.

00:03:28.567 --> 00:03:30.033
[ Laughter ]

00:03:30.033 --> 00:03:32.100
For this is a video tape of --

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:33.467
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.467 --> 00:03:35.100
of the defendant's
own confession.

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:36.300
[ Normal voice ] And then
there'll be, you know,

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:38.734
rumbling in the crowd
and the judge bangs gavel

00:03:38.734 --> 00:03:40.267
and say "Order in the court"
and the defense counsel,

00:03:40.267 --> 00:03:41.701
they'd be like, "Objection!
Where did you get that?"

00:03:41.701 --> 00:03:43.400
And then I would dramatic --
There would be dramatic music

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:44.467
and I would say,

00:03:44.467 --> 00:03:46.367
[ Southern drawl ]
"Well, I got this.

00:03:46.367 --> 00:03:48.367
[ Laughter ]

00:03:51.334 --> 00:03:54.267
This video tape?

00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:56.267
Oh, I'll tell you
where I got it.

00:03:56.267 --> 00:03:59.267
I got it from a C-SPAN!

00:03:59.267 --> 00:04:02.701
[ Dramatic music plays ]

00:04:02.701 --> 00:04:03.767
[ Applause ]

00:04:03.767 --> 00:04:05.534
[ Inaudible ]
...to rest this case."

00:04:05.534 --> 00:04:07.934
[ Applause ]

00:04:07.934 --> 00:04:09.667
[ Normal voice ] But let's stop
again and reflect on that.

00:04:09.667 --> 00:04:12.767
Trump's out there on camera
in front of a microphone

00:04:12.767 --> 00:04:14.634
bragging about
the size of the crowd,

00:04:14.634 --> 00:04:17.634
at an attempted violent coup
for which he is under

00:04:17.634 --> 00:04:19.567
multiple criminal
investigations currently.

00:04:19.567 --> 00:04:21.133
This is like
if during his trial,

00:04:21.133 --> 00:04:22.367
O.J. was also doing ads

00:04:22.367 --> 00:04:23.934
for a leather apparel company
with the slogan

00:04:23.934 --> 00:04:26.634
"When I do a hit,
I like to wear gloves fit."

00:04:26.634 --> 00:04:28.200
[ Laughter ]

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:30.567
It's like that.
That is what it is like.

00:04:30.567 --> 00:04:31.968
So that's why it's crucial

00:04:31.968 --> 00:04:33.601
to investigate
what happened on January 6th

00:04:33.601 --> 00:04:35.501
and hold the people
responsible, accountable.

00:04:35.501 --> 00:04:36.767
And that brings us
to today's hearing

00:04:36.767 --> 00:04:38.567
where the committee revealed
new evidence,

00:04:38.567 --> 00:04:40.334
including Secret Service
records,

00:04:40.334 --> 00:04:42.100
corroborating much of what
we already knew,

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:43.434
that Donald Trump was aware

00:04:43.434 --> 00:04:45.267
of the threat of violence
at the Capitol,

00:04:45.267 --> 00:04:48.133
and intentionally stoked it in
an attempt to stop congressmen

00:04:48.133 --> 00:04:49.767
certifying Joe Biden
as president.

00:04:49.767 --> 00:04:52.234
-Since the committee ended
their last hearing,

00:04:52.234 --> 00:04:53.934
the Department
of Homeland Security

00:04:53.934 --> 00:04:55.801
turned over a mountain
of new evidence,

00:04:55.801 --> 00:04:59.367
as you pointed out, over
a million different documents --

00:04:59.367 --> 00:05:01.300
a lot of other emails,

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:03.667
Microsoft teams
and communications

00:05:03.667 --> 00:05:05.133
between Secret Service agents

00:05:05.133 --> 00:05:07.100
and other administration
officials.

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:09.234
-Wait, you're telling me
the Secret Service

00:05:09.234 --> 00:05:13.167
and the Trump White House
used Microsoft teams?

00:05:13.167 --> 00:05:15.901
I'm willing to bet everything
I have that Donald Trump

00:05:15.901 --> 00:05:18.100
is one of those guys
who accidentally meets himself,

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:20.567
except he talks so much
you would never hear anyone else

00:05:20.567 --> 00:05:22.167
telling him to unmute.

00:05:22.167 --> 00:05:24.167
"Mr. President, we have warnings
from the Secret Service

00:05:24.167 --> 00:05:26.000
there will be violence
on January 6th."

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:27.801
[ mimics being on mute ]

00:05:27.801 --> 00:05:30.100
[ Laughter ]

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:32.767
"Mr. President, you need
to unmute yourself."

00:05:32.767 --> 00:05:34.067
[ Mute continues ]

00:05:34.067 --> 00:05:35.601
[ Laughter ]

00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:37.067
"Oh, God, no.

00:05:37.067 --> 00:05:39.767
I think he's talking about
how windmills kill birds again."

00:05:39.767 --> 00:05:41.767
[ Mute continues ]

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:45.400
[ Laughter ]

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:47.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:49.701 --> 00:05:50.968
"Oh, I don't want
to watch anymore.

00:05:50.968 --> 00:05:51.968
Let's just end this thing."

00:05:51.968 --> 00:05:55.200
Now, you might remember.

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:56.667
You might remember
in the last hearing,

00:05:56.667 --> 00:05:58.267
one of the many
stunning revelations

00:05:58.267 --> 00:06:01.367
was about Trump's actions
after his speech in January 6th.

00:06:01.367 --> 00:06:04.567
Before the riot, Trump wanted
to personally go to the Capitol

00:06:04.567 --> 00:06:05.834
to lead
the insurrection himself.

00:06:05.834 --> 00:06:07.133
And according to sworn testimony

00:06:07.133 --> 00:06:09.300
from former Trump aide
Cassidy Hutchinson,

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:12.434
Trump even went so far as to
assault a Secret Service officer

00:06:12.434 --> 00:06:15.234
and try to take command
of his presidential vehicle

00:06:15.234 --> 00:06:16.534
to drive it
to the insurrection himself.

00:06:16.534 --> 00:06:18.634
Now, a few days ago,
Trump denied that story,

00:06:18.634 --> 00:06:20.300
while also
simultaneously insisting

00:06:20.300 --> 00:06:22.634
that if it was true,
it would make him look cool.

00:06:22.634 --> 00:06:26.000
-If you listen to this one
very sick individual,

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:28.334
in order to get
the Secret Service

00:06:28.334 --> 00:06:30.400
to take me to the Capitol,

00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:33.167
I grabbed one
around the neck

00:06:33.167 --> 00:06:34.534
and I --

00:06:34.534 --> 00:06:36.634
and, you know, I almost
didn't want to dispute it

00:06:36.634 --> 00:06:37.834
because a lot of people said,

00:06:37.834 --> 00:06:39.567
I never knew you were
that physically tough.

00:06:39.567 --> 00:06:40.834
[ Laughter ]

00:06:40.834 --> 00:06:43.300
This guy was a tough guy
that I supposedly grabbed.

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:44.701
If I grabbed him
around the neck,

00:06:44.701 --> 00:06:46.601
I think I would have been
in serious trouble.

00:06:46.601 --> 00:06:48.300
-I mean, you are.

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:49.400
[ Laughter ]

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:50.801
-You are in serious trouble.

00:06:50.801 --> 00:06:53.267
You're under like 19 different
criminal investigations

00:06:53.267 --> 00:06:54.400
and you just got subpoenaed.

00:06:54.400 --> 00:06:55.534
But I do know what he means.

00:06:55.534 --> 00:06:56.667
He means he would have

00:06:56.667 --> 00:06:58.300
physically been
in serious trouble.

00:06:58.300 --> 00:06:59.801
Not that I think
a Secret Service agent,

00:06:59.801 --> 00:07:02.300
whatever body slam Trump,
I mean, they definitely could,

00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:04.701
but they got to know he would
sue that [ Bleep ] out of them.

00:07:04.701 --> 00:07:08.000
I mean, even if he was fine,
you know Trump would start

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:10.200
showing up to press conferences
in a fake neck brace

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:12.167
so he could take
the Secret Service to court.

00:07:12.167 --> 00:07:13.334
[ As Trump ] I apologize,

00:07:13.334 --> 00:07:15.334
but I'd only be taking
questions from those you

00:07:15.334 --> 00:07:17.000
in my direct line of sight.

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:18.100
[ Laughter ]

00:07:18.100 --> 00:07:20.834
You know, due to the incident.

00:07:20.834 --> 00:07:22.634
[ Laughter ]

00:07:22.634 --> 00:07:25.234
[ Normal voice ] I don't think
it would take much

00:07:25.234 --> 00:07:27.400
for a Secret Service agent
to subdue Donald Trump.

00:07:27.400 --> 00:07:29.467
You probably only have to,
like, hold his nose closed

00:07:29.467 --> 00:07:31.367
for 5 to 10 seconds.

00:07:31.367 --> 00:07:32.567
And because
he won't stop talking,

00:07:32.567 --> 00:07:34.400
he passes out
from lack of oxygen.

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:36.067
[ As Trump ] You messed
with the wrong president,

00:07:36.067 --> 00:07:37.400
you son of a --

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:38.667
[ Laughter ]

00:07:38.667 --> 00:07:40.000
[ Normal voice ] He's out.

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:41.701
It'd be like that thing
where your sugared-up nephew

00:07:41.701 --> 00:07:44.267
thinks it's funny to hit you
so you just hold his wrists

00:07:44.267 --> 00:07:47.033
and wait for your sister to look
up from her [ Bleep ] phone

00:07:47.033 --> 00:07:48.534
and do some parenting
for a change.

00:07:48.534 --> 00:07:50.033
Abby!

00:07:50.033 --> 00:07:52.033
[ Laughter ]

00:07:53.234 --> 00:07:55.968
But thanks to new communications
revealed today by the committee,

00:07:55.968 --> 00:07:57.567
we now have proof
that the Secret Service

00:07:57.567 --> 00:07:59.000
was communicating in real time

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:01.968
about whether they could stop
Trump from going to the capital,

00:08:01.968 --> 00:08:03.467
and leading our mob
as he attempted

00:08:03.467 --> 00:08:04.901
to violently
overthrow the government.

00:08:04.901 --> 00:08:06.834
-One of the committee's newly
obtained documents

00:08:06.834 --> 00:08:09.167
shows that sometime between
1:30 and 2:00 p.m.,

00:08:09.167 --> 00:08:10.968
a senior
Secret Service supervisor

00:08:10.968 --> 00:08:12.634
for protective operations

00:08:12.634 --> 00:08:15.901
emailed Trump's Security Detail
leader Bobby Engel

00:08:15.901 --> 00:08:18.400
with an urgent update seeking
to know of Trump's plan

00:08:18.400 --> 00:08:20.968
to go to the Capitol
was successfully quashed.

00:08:20.968 --> 00:08:23.934
It came after a tumultuous hour
for the Secret Service detail,

00:08:23.934 --> 00:08:26.701
which had effectively ignored
a command from the president,

00:08:26.701 --> 00:08:28.767
which was to go down
to the insurrection.

00:08:28.767 --> 00:08:30.000
Even with Trump back
at the White House,

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:31.334
Secret Service headquarters
wanted to be sure

00:08:31.334 --> 00:08:32.467
the president was staying put.

00:08:32.467 --> 00:08:33.968
-That's right.
The Secret Service ignored

00:08:33.968 --> 00:08:35.834
a command from the president
to go to the Capitol

00:08:35.834 --> 00:08:36.968
to lead the armed mob.

00:08:36.968 --> 00:08:38.367
And then they communicated
back and forth

00:08:38.367 --> 00:08:41.067
about whether Trump's plan
had been successfully quashed.

00:08:41.067 --> 00:08:42.300
I really wish we could see

00:08:42.300 --> 00:08:44.534
all those specific
text messages.

00:09:05.267 --> 00:09:07.334
The committee also made clear
to point out

00:09:07.334 --> 00:09:10.033
that the evidence they provided
so far has not been partisan.

00:09:10.033 --> 00:09:12.734
In fact, most of it
has been provided by Republicans

00:09:12.734 --> 00:09:14.567
and people close
to Donald Trump himself.

00:09:14.567 --> 00:09:19.634
-All this evidence come almost
entirely from Republicans.

00:09:19.634 --> 00:09:23.667
The evidence that has emerged
did not come from Democrats

00:09:23.667 --> 00:09:26.000
or opponents of Donald Trump.

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:29.868
Instead, look at who's written
and testified

00:09:29.868 --> 00:09:33.767
and produced evidence.
Who has that been?

00:09:33.767 --> 00:09:37.534
Aides who've worked loyally
for Donald Trump for years.

00:09:37.534 --> 00:09:40.534
Republican state officials
and legislators.

00:09:40.534 --> 00:09:42.400
Republican electors.

00:09:42.400 --> 00:09:46.133
The chairwoman of the
Republican National Committee.

00:09:46.133 --> 00:09:49.934
Political professionals who
worked at the highest levels

00:09:49.934 --> 00:09:51.968
of the Trump campaign.

00:09:51.968 --> 00:09:56.100
Trump appointees who served
in the most senior positions

00:09:56.100 --> 00:09:58.234
in the Justice Department.

00:09:58.234 --> 00:10:00.033
President Trump's staff

00:10:00.033 --> 00:10:03.267
and closest advisers
in the White House.

00:10:03.267 --> 00:10:05.767
Members of
President Trump's family.

00:10:05.767 --> 00:10:07.534
-That's right.
Even Trump's own family

00:10:07.534 --> 00:10:09.667
provided damning testimony
about the attempted coup.

00:10:09.667 --> 00:10:11.467
There were text messages
from Don Jr.

00:10:11.467 --> 00:10:13.434
There was video testimony
from Ivanka.

00:10:13.434 --> 00:10:15.067
There was even appearance
from that ghost

00:10:15.067 --> 00:10:16.701
Trump befriended
during an audition --

00:10:16.701 --> 00:10:17.901
[ Laughter ]

00:10:17.901 --> 00:10:19.334
an audition
for the movie "Smile,"

00:10:19.334 --> 00:10:21.467
which neither of them
got cast in

00:10:21.467 --> 00:10:23.200
because they're just not
capable of smiling.

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:24.501
The best Jared Kushner
is capable of

00:10:24.501 --> 00:10:25.801
is making a pained sneer,

00:10:25.801 --> 00:10:27.801
like he just smelled
one of Trump's KFC farts.

00:10:27.801 --> 00:10:29.067
[ Laughter ]

00:10:29.067 --> 00:10:30.934
Committee Chairman
Bennie Thompson also mentioned

00:10:30.934 --> 00:10:33.167
that some of the testimony
came from Trump allies

00:10:33.167 --> 00:10:35.000
who did not necessarily
want to testify

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:36.400
but ended up complying anyway.

00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:38.234
-And I want to be clear,

00:10:38.234 --> 00:10:41.834
not all these witnesses
were thrilled to talk to us.

00:10:41.834 --> 00:10:44.300
Some of them put up
quite a fight.

00:10:44.300 --> 00:10:47.934
But ultimately,
the vast majority cooperated

00:10:47.934 --> 00:10:49.534
with our investigation.

00:10:49.534 --> 00:10:50.834
-Oh, they put up a fight,
all right.

00:10:50.834 --> 00:10:52.167
In fact, Rudy Giuliani
even tried

00:10:52.167 --> 00:10:53.567
swinging a golf club at us,

00:10:53.567 --> 00:10:56.968
but he got tangled up in his
super long khaki golf short.

00:10:56.968 --> 00:10:58.133
So we had to untangle him.

00:10:58.133 --> 00:11:00.501
But then he got his head
stuck in the golf shorts,

00:11:00.501 --> 00:11:01.934
so we had to bring
in the Jaws of Life

00:11:01.934 --> 00:11:03.100
to cut him out of the shorts.

00:11:03.100 --> 00:11:05.200
But then it turned out
he had a second pair

00:11:05.200 --> 00:11:07.133
of even longer shorts
under the first pair of shorts,

00:11:07.133 --> 00:11:09.901
so then we had that --
we just let him go home.

00:11:09.901 --> 00:11:12.100
And then, in an especially
attention-grabbing moment,

00:11:12.100 --> 00:11:13.601
the committee hinted
at the possibility

00:11:13.601 --> 00:11:15.467
of holding
some of the figures involved

00:11:15.467 --> 00:11:17.067
in the coup
criminally accountable.

00:11:17.067 --> 00:11:19.467
-We've received new
witness testimony,

00:11:19.467 --> 00:11:22.200
including about efforts
to obstruct

00:11:22.200 --> 00:11:25.801
our investigation
and conceal key facts.

00:11:25.801 --> 00:11:27.601
And according to
public reporting,

00:11:27.601 --> 00:11:29.868
the Department of Justice
has been very active

00:11:29.868 --> 00:11:32.434
in pursuing many
of the issues identified

00:11:32.434 --> 00:11:34.701
in our prior hearings.

00:11:34.701 --> 00:11:36.567
Our committee
may ultimately decide

00:11:36.567 --> 00:11:38.434
to make a series
of criminal referrals

00:11:38.434 --> 00:11:39.834
to the Department of Justice.

00:11:39.834 --> 00:11:42.067
-You might end up
making criminal referrals?

00:11:42.067 --> 00:11:44.234
What else has to happen
to make a criminal referral?

00:11:44.234 --> 00:11:46.300
I mean, if only we had
Donald Trump on video

00:11:46.300 --> 00:11:47.634
inciting a riot or,
I don't know,

00:11:47.634 --> 00:11:49.200
bragging about the size
of the violent crowd

00:11:49.200 --> 00:11:50.567
he whipped up
to storm the Capitol

00:11:50.567 --> 00:11:51.934
and overthrow democracy.

00:11:51.934 --> 00:11:54.601
And if only we had a cunning,
amiable Southern lawyer

00:11:54.601 --> 00:11:57.734
brave enough
to show up to the hearing

00:11:57.734 --> 00:12:01.033
and present the court
with the "vidja" tape.

00:12:01.033 --> 00:12:04.367
[ Dramatic music sting ]

00:12:04.367 --> 00:12:08.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:12:08.467 --> 00:12:10.634
Shoemaker, send it to NBC.

00:12:10.634 --> 00:12:12.601
I think they're gonna pick up
"Southern Lawyer."

00:12:12.601 --> 00:12:15.534
[ Laughter ]

00:12:15.534 --> 00:12:18.000
I also --
"Chicago Southern Lawyer."

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:19.467
[ Laughter ]

00:12:19.467 --> 00:12:20.834
I also think
one of the most notable

00:12:20.834 --> 00:12:22.167
revelations in the hearing today

00:12:22.167 --> 00:12:24.367
was the fact that Trump
actually admitted privately

00:12:24.367 --> 00:12:26.300
to several of his aides
that he knew he lost

00:12:26.300 --> 00:12:27.667
and decided to lie
to his supporters

00:12:27.667 --> 00:12:28.801
and the country anyway

00:12:28.801 --> 00:12:30.601
in order
to orchestrate his violent coup.

00:12:30.601 --> 00:12:32.767
-At times,
President Trump acknowledged

00:12:32.767 --> 00:12:35.100
the reality of his loss,

00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:37.868
Although he publicly claimed
that he had won the election,

00:12:37.868 --> 00:12:40.400
privately, he admitted
that Joe Biden

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:41.767
would take over as president.

00:12:41.767 --> 00:12:44.767
Here's a few examples of that.

00:12:44.767 --> 00:12:45.801
-So, we're in the Oval,

00:12:45.801 --> 00:12:47.767
and there's a discussion
going on.

00:12:47.767 --> 00:12:50.167
And the President says,

00:12:50.167 --> 00:12:51.601
I think it could
have been Pompeo,

00:12:51.601 --> 00:12:54.167
but he says words
to the effect of,

00:12:54.167 --> 00:12:56.434
"Yeah, we lost.
We need to let that issue

00:12:56.434 --> 00:12:59.901
go to the next guy,"
meaning President Biden.

00:12:59.901 --> 00:13:04.000
-I remember maybe a week
after the election was called,

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:05.434
I popped into the Oval

00:13:05.434 --> 00:13:07.834
just to, like,
give the President the headlines

00:13:07.834 --> 00:13:09.167
and see how he was doing.

00:13:09.167 --> 00:13:10.601
And he was looking at the TV,
and he said,

00:13:10.601 --> 00:13:13.200
"Can you believe
I lost to this f'ing guy?"

00:13:13.200 --> 00:13:15.567
-Mark raised it with me
on the 18th.

00:13:15.567 --> 00:13:17.767
And so following
that conversation

00:13:17.767 --> 00:13:21.133
with the motorcade ride
driving back to the White House,

00:13:21.133 --> 00:13:22.300
and I said,
"Like, does the President

00:13:22.300 --> 00:13:24.734
really think that he lost?"

00:13:24.734 --> 00:13:27.868
And he said, "A lot of times
he'll tell me that he lost,

00:13:27.868 --> 00:13:29.300
but he wants
to keep fighting it.

00:13:29.300 --> 00:13:31.734
He thinks that there might be
enough to overturn the election.

00:13:31.734 --> 00:13:33.467
But, you know, he --
he pretty much

00:13:33.467 --> 00:13:35.834
has acknowledged
that he -- that he's lost."

00:13:35.834 --> 00:13:38.100
-That's right. Trump admitted
multiple times in private

00:13:38.100 --> 00:13:40.133
that he had lost and even said
at one point of Biden,

00:13:40.133 --> 00:13:42.067
"Can you believe
I lost to this [bleep] guy?"

00:13:42.067 --> 00:13:44.567
Trump being shocked that he lost
is like your dad being shocked

00:13:44.567 --> 00:13:45.734
that the Motorola flip phone

00:13:45.734 --> 00:13:48.834
he still has
gets [bleep] service.

00:13:48.834 --> 00:13:50.234
"I can't hear
a word you're saying.

00:13:50.234 --> 00:13:52.167
This thing sucks. Here.
Talk to your mother."

00:13:52.167 --> 00:13:54.133
"I'll call you on my phone.
Bye."

00:13:54.133 --> 00:13:55.367
[ Laughter ]

00:13:55.367 --> 00:13:56.868
So Trump knew that he lost.

00:13:56.868 --> 00:13:59.400
He concocted an elaborate lie to
save himself from embarrassment.

00:13:59.400 --> 00:14:01.567
In fact, he said as much
when the Supreme Court rejected

00:14:01.567 --> 00:14:03.734
his last-ditch attempt
to overturn the results.

00:14:03.734 --> 00:14:06.133
Private Secret Service messages
and testimony

00:14:06.133 --> 00:14:07.901
from former Trump aide
Cassidy Hutchinson

00:14:07.901 --> 00:14:09.434
revealed that Trump
was embarrassed he lost

00:14:09.434 --> 00:14:10.701
and wanted to cover it up.

00:14:10.701 --> 00:14:13.133
-On December 11th,
Trump's allies lost a lawsuit

00:14:13.133 --> 00:14:14.934
in the U.S. Supreme Court

00:14:14.934 --> 00:14:19.667
that he regarded as his last
chance at success in the courts.

00:14:19.667 --> 00:14:22.734
A newly obtained Secret Service
message from that day

00:14:22.734 --> 00:14:26.534
shows how angry President Trump
was about the outcome.

00:14:26.534 --> 00:14:31.300
Quote,
"Just FYI -- POTUS is pissed.

00:14:31.300 --> 00:14:34.100
Breaking news -- Supreme Court
denied his lawsuit.

00:14:34.100 --> 00:14:36.000
He is livid now."

00:14:36.000 --> 00:14:38.734
Cassidy Hutchinson, an aide
to chief of staff

00:14:38.734 --> 00:14:41.767
Mark Meadows, was present
for that conversation

00:14:41.767 --> 00:14:43.767
and described it in this way.

00:14:43.767 --> 00:14:46.934
-The President just raging about
the decision and how it's wrong

00:14:46.934 --> 00:14:48.634
and why didn't
we make more calls

00:14:48.634 --> 00:14:54.133
and just his typical

00:14:54.133 --> 00:14:56.467
anger outburst at this decision.

00:14:56.467 --> 00:15:02.033
And the President said --
He --

00:15:02.033 --> 00:15:05.000
So, he had said something
to the effect of,

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:06.701
"I don't want people
to know we lost, Mark.

00:15:06.701 --> 00:15:08.300
This is embarrassing.

00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:09.767
Figure it out.
We need to figure it out.

00:15:09.767 --> 00:15:11.934
I don't want people to know
that we lost."

00:15:11.934 --> 00:15:14.200
-First of all, I like that even
the Secret Service was saying,

00:15:14.200 --> 00:15:15.601
"Yikes, this dude is pissed.

00:15:15.601 --> 00:15:18.000
You think the Secret Service
is completely silent

00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:19.367
with no personality whatsoever,

00:15:19.367 --> 00:15:22.033
but it turns out,
they're actually huge gossips.

00:15:22.033 --> 00:15:24.000
"Oh, my God.
Did you hear Donald Trump

00:15:24.000 --> 00:15:25.701
totally chewed out Rudy
at the meeting today?

00:15:25.701 --> 00:15:28.434
He also came up with
a new nickname for Mike Pence.

00:15:28.434 --> 00:15:30.634
He called them Mike...

00:15:30.634 --> 00:15:31.634
[ Quietly ] ...Penis."

00:15:31.634 --> 00:15:34.133
[ Laughter ]

00:15:34.133 --> 00:15:36.033
So Trump knew he lost
and was just embarrassed,

00:15:36.033 --> 00:15:37.567
so we decided to concoct
an elaborate

00:15:37.567 --> 00:15:38.834
lie about supposed fraud

00:15:38.834 --> 00:15:41.067
and orchestrate a violent scheme
to overturn the results.

00:15:41.067 --> 00:15:42.234
You know,
you'd think at this point

00:15:42.234 --> 00:15:43.901
Trump would be used
to being embarrassed.

00:15:43.901 --> 00:15:45.300
This is a man who,
let's not forget,

00:15:45.300 --> 00:15:46.834
once got on Air Force One
with toilet paper

00:15:46.834 --> 00:15:47.868
stuck to his shoe

00:15:47.868 --> 00:15:49.968
and went outside
looking like this.

00:15:49.968 --> 00:15:53.200
He looks like he heard a rumor
the Democrats were hiding

00:15:53.200 --> 00:15:54.467
fake ballots
in microwaves,

00:15:54.467 --> 00:15:57.067
so he stuck his head inside
one to investigate.

00:15:57.067 --> 00:16:01.467
"No ballots in here.
All I found is a frozen burrito.

00:16:01.467 --> 00:16:02.501
Where is the burrito?

00:16:02.501 --> 00:16:04.901
I regret to inform you
it is gone."

00:16:04.901 --> 00:16:06.501
[ Laughter ]

00:16:06.501 --> 00:16:08.667
"I ate the burrito."
[ Laughter ]

00:16:08.667 --> 00:16:10.667
Today's hearing provided
yet more evidence

00:16:10.667 --> 00:16:12.834
that Trump knew he lost
and concocted an elaborate lie

00:16:12.834 --> 00:16:13.701
to stay in power.

00:16:13.701 --> 00:16:14.968
He orchestrated a violent coup,

00:16:14.968 --> 00:16:16.834
and if we don't hold him
and his cronies accountable

00:16:16.834 --> 00:16:18.634
for this one,
he's just gonna do it again,

00:16:18.634 --> 00:16:20.133
because as today's
hearings brew,

00:16:20.133 --> 00:16:21.200
Donald Trump is one...

00:16:21.200 --> 00:16:22.734
-Very sick individual.

00:16:22.734 --> 00:16:24.834
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

